Codifies accepted Bucket-I implementation-conformance gaps (docs/SPEC_GAP_PROPOSALS.md
in scrimshawlife-ctrl/SUAS) into the canonical logical model. All additive and
backward-compatible; no new product/domain behavior is invented.

- DATA_MODEL.md: notifications subject_type/subject_id (P-12); follow_ups
  responsible_type enum + referral_id (P-14); suas_admin_grants record (P-15);
  fulfillment reconciliation sub-state + assignment/fulfillment cardinality
  (P-16); support_cases.priority_signal_level (P-22); effective-signal
  selection rule (P-21).
- NOTIFICATIONS.md §3: subject reference (P-12).
- RESOURCES.md §2: contact_method_kind scheme discriminator (P-13).
- REFERRALS.md §2: typed {destination_type,destination_id} (P-13).
- AUTH.md §6: SUAS_ADMIN as auditable grant record (P-15).
